{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Closing as a DUPLICATE of longish-ripe-snowyowl (2331-3e0e-f880-4837), which was filed first for the same defect and is referenced from the study's results document. All evidence from this ticket — the 11-run totals, the 24 duplicate groups, the fingerprint finding, the three drop reasons, the blocking counts and the divergent blocking eligibility — has been consolidated onto that ticket as a comment. Linked `duplicates`.\n\nWhy this happened, recorded because it is a search hazard others will hit: I searched the tracker before filing and concluded no such bug existed. The existing ticket's title does contain \"duplicates\", so a title filter should have matched it — but it was not in the result set my full-text search returned at all. I filtered a capped/ranked result list and treated it as the whole corpus. A negative result from `rebar search` is not proof of absence."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789504348805635001,"uuid":"1a9506f3-1c2b-4ab2-b87c-324d0457c450"}